    "name": "Pay with saved card",
    "description": "## Overview\n\nPaymob facilitates seamless payments by allowing users to transact with saved card tokens, which enable transactions using previously stored cards.\n\n**Payment Approaches**\n\nThere are **two approaches** for implementing saved token payments, depending on who initiates the transaction:\n\n### 1\\. CIT (Customer Initiated Transaction)\n\nCustomer-driven payments where the cardholder is present and actively participates in the checkout process. The customer only needs to enter their CVV to complete the payment with their saved card.\n\n### 2\\. MIT (Merchant Initiated Transaction)\n\nMerchant-driven payments where transactions occur without direct customer involvement at the time of payment. The merchant processes the payment using the saved token via API.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n**Before using either CIT or MIT, you must:**\n\n1. Complete the **Create Card Token** process to obtain a customer's saved card token\n    \n2. Store this token securely in your database\n    \n3. Have the appropriate integration IDs configured in your Paymob dashboard",
